Monshiro MS

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:46.160
Before we knew it...

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:47.080
We won!

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:49.790
We did it!

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:49.790
Even though we only have eight players!

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:53.540
Yuni, great job getting that one hit.

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:57.450
I know, right? I just can't keep
my eyes off the ball today.

00:10:57.450 --> 00:10:59.080
Also, whenever I saw the other team's faces,

00:10:59.080 --> 00:11:02.410
I could sorta figure out
what they were thinking.

00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:07.080
What the hell? Talkin' big like that.
You're gonna make me fall for you.

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:09.580
Hey, Teach. Do you know where Haijima is?

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:11.410
He went back inside.

00:11:11.410 --> 00:11:14.990
The second game on Court A is gonna start soon.

00:11:14.990 --> 00:11:18.910
That game's gonna decide who
we play next, so he went to watch.

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:21.160
He didn't have to go himself.

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:26.330
Haijima was probably being nice
and letting you guys rest.

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:32.870
Man... I knew Haijima had some experience,
but I didn't know he was that good.

00:11:32.870 --> 00:11:39.450
I just had a bunch of the coaches
from other schools ask me who he was.

00:11:39.450 --> 00:11:42.910
Hey, what about me? Did anyone ask about me?

00:11:42.910 --> 00:11:45.790
Hmm... Nope, don't think so.

00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:49.580
Haijima's taking all the glory here.

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:52.120
You'll get your time to shine soon.

00:11:52.120 --> 00:11:55.080
All right, keep this up
for our second game, too.

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:57.490
Just go out there and have fun.

00:11:57.490 --> 00:11:59.200
Right!

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:03.830
Just two more. If we win two more...

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:15.080
O-Out?

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:16.330
Don't worry about it.

00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:19.080
He's not even worried about missing a serve.

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:20.700
Even if we get a point,

00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:23.950
he knows how intimidating
a spike serve is to our team...

00:12:23.950 --> 00:12:28.330
That Haijima kid is definitely experienced.

00:12:28.330 --> 00:12:29.990
Hey! Kuroba!

00:12:31.990 --> 00:12:34.120
Wait, I'm still on the left?

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:35.240
Wake up!

00:12:35.240 --> 00:12:37.290
S-Sorry.

00:12:37.290 --> 00:12:42.120
Wh-What's going on? My body feels super anxious.

00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:44.790
Am I nervous? Why?

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:46.830
Tahara MS

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:46.830
Monshiro MS

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:49.990
Get a grip. We're in the middle of a match.

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:53.540
I just need to get the serve in
like I usually do...

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:55.740
Wait...

00:12:55.740 --> 00:13:00.540
What foot do I usually step off with?
When do I toss the ball up?

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:03.290
How do I usually do this?

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:06.990
An 8-second violation?

00:13:07.990 --> 00:13:10.660
T-Time out!

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:13.120
You're nervous, aren't you?

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:15.620
Do you get nervous when you're put on the spot?

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:21.080
I've never really been put on
the spot before, so I'm not sure.

00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:23.330
Well, figure out a way to calm down.

00:13:23.330 --> 00:13:25.990
Couldn't you give better advice than that?

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:28.330
I've never been nervous.

00:13:28.330 --> 00:13:30.790
I can help you out with plays, but that's it.

00:13:30.790 --> 00:13:34.490
Look, Yuni. I'm nervous, too.

00:13:34.490 --> 00:13:36.370
Try not to worry about messing up.

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:38.120
R-Right.

00:13:40.580 --> 00:13:42.540
A pipe attack...

00:13:44.870 --> 00:13:46.200
A back row attack...

00:13:47.410 --> 00:13:49.160
Wait, there's a wall?

00:13:51.490 --> 00:13:53.080
Wh-What?

00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:55.870
What's wrong, Yuni?

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:55.870
--Nice!
--All right!

00:13:56.410 --> 00:13:58.740
Tahara MS

00:13:56.410 --> 00:13:58.740
Monshiro MS

00:14:04.950 --> 00:14:06.330
Why?

00:14:06.330 --> 00:14:07.910
Why is it just me?

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:15.080
The blockers keep concentrating on me.

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:16.660
Sorry.

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:18.330
That was unavoidable.

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:21.580
They figured out that you're the only one
who can get a decent hit over.

00:14:21.580 --> 00:14:23.330
We'll try to get it down to one blocker,

00:14:23.330 --> 00:14:24.870
so just calm down and watch them.

00:14:24.870 --> 00:14:28.370
You can get past their blocks.

00:14:28.370 --> 00:14:29.620
Are you listening?

00:14:29.620 --> 00:14:32.490
R-Right...

00:14:32.490 --> 00:14:35.450
Calm down and watch the blockers.

00:14:35.450 --> 00:14:38.240
Watch the blockers. Watch the...

00:14:38.240 --> 00:14:39.240
Yuni!

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:48.580
Why? Why can't I get it over?

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:54.700
Am I not jumping high enough? Am I exhausted?

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:58.450
My body feels heavy. I felt so light earlier.

00:14:58.450 --> 00:15:02.120
What should I do? What do I... What...

00:15:02.120 --> 00:15:05.990
Someone say something. What should I...

00:15:14.490 --> 00:15:16.200
You're useless.

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:19.700
How?

00:15:19.700 --> 00:15:22.150
Tahara MS

00:15:19.700 --> 00:15:22.150
Monshiro MS

00:15:19.700 --> 00:15:22.490
How did we win?

00:15:22.490 --> 00:15:27.080
I stopped touching the ball at some point.

00:15:27.080 --> 00:15:31.080
Haijima- <i>senpai</i> was a monster on that court.

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:32.290
That's right.

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:36.080
At some point, Haijima changed up his plays.

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:43.330
He started using dumps...

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:47.290
Once they figured that out,
he started going after rebounds.

00:15:47.290 --> 00:15:47.920
Get the ball up!

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:49.410
R-Right!

00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:57.330
Then he got one spike serve in after another.

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:03.100
Tahara MS

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:03.100
Monshiro MS

00:16:00.950 --> 00:16:03.700
He kept scoring on his own.

00:16:03.700 --> 00:16:07.660
He was playing the game all by himself.

00:16:07.660 --> 00:16:10.120
I guess you can actually play like that...

00:16:10.120 --> 00:16:14.450
How is he so good?

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:17.450
What the heck is even the point

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:21.040
of us being on that court?

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:27.080
I need to make sure I cheer my heart out for him

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:29.910
so he can get back on his game tomorrow.

00:16:31.910 --> 00:16:34.450
You've got this, Yuni...

00:16:34.450 --> 00:16:37.120
Hey, Ryo. It's me.

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:40.580
About today's game...

00:16:40.580 --> 00:16:44.700
What's Yuni doing? It's past the meet-up time.

00:16:44.700 --> 00:16:46.080
What'd his family say?

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:49.200
They said he left the house.

00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:53.580
Was Yuni- <i>senpai</i> in some kind of accident?

00:16:53.580 --> 00:16:57.080
You dummy. Don't say stuff like that.

00:16:57.080 --> 00:16:58.370
Tomita

00:16:57.080 --> 00:16:58.370
Hospital

00:16:57.080 --> 00:16:58.620
Oh?

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:00.700
You actually came to see me?

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:02.120
The hell?

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:03.790
You seem fine.

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:05.830
The hell'd you do?

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:10.910
I spent all night making this flag and
was gonna take it over to the gym on my bike,

00:17:10.910 --> 00:17:14.540
but then I lost my balance, ended up
in a ditch, and sprained my ankle.

00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:19.970
"Fly Kuroba Universe"

00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:20.200
Are you stupid? Of course you'd fall
off your bike holding a flag this big.

00:17:20.200 --> 00:17:24.790
Oh, so you just sprained your ankle.
I can't believe we rushed over here.

00:17:24.790 --> 00:17:28.080
Yuni, isn't your game starting soon?

00:17:28.080 --> 00:17:30.830
What are you doing here?

00:17:30.830 --> 00:17:33.540
I just happened to run into Yori on the way

00:17:33.540 --> 00:17:34.950
and heard they took you to the hospital.

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:39.990
And as you can see, I'm fine.
So hurry up and get to your match!

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:43.450
But it starts in five minutes,
so I'm not gonna make it in time.

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:46.910
And as long as Haijima's there...

00:17:46.910 --> 00:17:49.450
H-Hey, your foot...

00:17:49.450 --> 00:17:51.450
Quit your whining

00:17:51.450 --> 00:17:53.080
and get your ass to the game!

00:17:56.740 --> 00:18:00.950
Even if we hurry, we won't
get there until after 10:30.

00:18:00.950 --> 00:18:02.740
Say, Yori.

00:18:02.740 --> 00:18:05.450
Remember when you told me a bunch
of guys from Haijima's school in Tokyo

00:18:05.450 --> 00:18:09.290
had written bad things about him online?

00:18:09.290 --> 00:18:12.950
Huh? Yeah.

00:18:12.950 --> 00:18:16.540
I ended up doing the same thing.

00:18:16.540 --> 00:18:19.910
Last night, I ended up
calling our other teammates,

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:22.790
and we talked shit about him.

00:18:22.790 --> 00:18:24.790
I see.

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:27.620
As long as Haijima's there,
he can basically win the match himself.

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:32.700
He doesn't need me. Honestly,
I didn't want to be in the game.

00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:36.830
I basically went with you to see Itoko

00:18:36.830 --> 00:18:42.330
so it'd give me an excuse not to play the game.

00:18:42.330 --> 00:18:45.200
I see.

00:18:45.200 --> 00:18:48.830
What the hell...

00:18:48.830 --> 00:18:50.950
...was I even trying to do?

00:20:23.160 --> 00:20:24.990
We lost?

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:28.830
No way... It's only been an hour
since the game started.

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:32.120
I wouldn't lie about that.
We lost in the semi-finals.

00:20:32.120 --> 00:20:34.410
We forfeited the match to decide third place.

00:20:34.410 --> 00:20:37.200
Everyone already went home.

00:20:37.200 --> 00:20:41.200
What... But why? Haijima was here,
so we should've won like yesterday...

00:20:41.200 --> 00:20:42.490
Are you stupid?

00:20:42.490 --> 00:20:47.620
Our team definitely needs Haijima,
but there's no way he could win on his own.

00:20:47.620 --> 00:20:51.240
There's a rule in volleyball
where the same player

00:20:51.240 --> 00:20:52.830
can't touch the ball twice in a row.

00:20:52.830 --> 00:20:56.240
You didn't know that?
Do you need the damn rulebook?

00:20:57.830 --> 00:21:02.410
You didn't talk to Haijima yesterday?

00:21:02.410 --> 00:21:09.330
Even Haijima knew what he did yesterday
was basically like a surprise attack.

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:12.580
He knew it wouldn't work again today.

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:17.410
But he thought we could win as long
as you could pick yourself back up again.

00:21:17.410 --> 00:21:19.160
Haijima said that?

00:21:19.160 --> 00:21:20.990
Well, you know how he is.

00:21:20.990 --> 00:21:23.910
Even though you weren't here,
he put on a strong front,

00:21:23.910 --> 00:21:27.080
But then he hurt himself
in the middle of the first set.

00:21:27.080 --> 00:21:32.490
I figured something was off,
but he never showed it.

00:21:32.490 --> 00:21:35.950
Hey, Haijima. What'd they say?

00:21:35.950 --> 00:21:39.370
I'd dislocated my middle finger
on my right hand.

00:21:39.370 --> 00:21:42.450
We're gonna take a taxi
to the hospital. Come on.

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:47.910
Oh, so you are alive.

00:21:47.910 --> 00:21:50.790
Haijima. I-I...

00:21:51.870 --> 00:21:54.790
You made it loud and clear what you think of me.

00:21:54.790 --> 00:21:57.660
Don't worry. It's over.

00:21:57.660 --> 00:22:00.950
This jackass pushed another teammate
over the edge for not listening to him,

00:22:00.950 --> 00:22:03.200
and the kid tried to take his own life.

00:22:03.200 --> 00:22:06.870
I'll decide what I think about you myself.

00:22:06.870 --> 00:22:10.830
But he thought we could win as long as
you could pick yourself back up again.

00:22:12.450 --> 00:22:16.620
Is this... the end? Is it really the end?

00:22:16.620 --> 00:22:21.410
Did I end our final middle-school
tournament like this?

00:22:22.830 --> 00:22:28.910
It was my fault we were
off our game and I just gave up...

00:22:28.910 --> 00:22:35.450
Even then, you wanted to do everything
you could to let us win, and we did...

00:22:35.450 --> 00:22:41.700
And yet I had the nerve to sulk
and talk shit about you...

00:22:43.240 --> 00:22:45.910
Don't worry. It's over.

00:22:48.290 --> 00:22:51.950
I don't want it to end. Not like this.

00:22:53.950 --> 00:22:57.660
I still... I still...

00:22:57.660 --> 00:23:01.240
...want to play volleyball with Haijima.
